# Integration tests write their key material and round-trip files straight into
# tests/ rather than a tempdir, so a plain `cargo test` leaves private keys in
# the worktree. Ignore them: jj auto-tracks anything not listed here, which is
# how they nearly ended up in a commit.
#
# Match the prefixes, not the leaf names. Enumerating leaf names has already
# missed three working directories -- tests/interop_data/ (tests/interop.rs),
# tests/temp_security/ and tests/temp_encrypted_key/ (tests/security.rs) -- and
# cleanup runs on the success path only, so a failing assertion leaves the keys
# behind. tests/temp_* also covers the e2e/threat suites and tests/tmp_* the
# KeyBundle ones (tests/keybundle_cli.rs: expired, wrongpin, rawgate, keyring,
# genmykey).
tests/temp_*/
tests/tmp_*/
tests/interop_data/
tests/input_*
tests/output_*
# Belt and braces for whatever the next suite names its directory: no private
# key material anywhere under tests/, regardless of the directory it lands in.
tests/**/*.key
# ...except the fixtures, which are committed on purpose as test vectors.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.key

# Network chat test artifacts
ticket.txt
ticket.log

# Generated UniFFI bindings (regenerate with the uniffi-bindgen bin)
/bindings/
demos/.state/

# Reproducible-build output (the artifact + SHA256SUMS are published per release,
